title: The Republic at Two
subtitle: Recovery or hunger?
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dix >= 72 and bol_regime = 0
priority: 20
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.recovered = (Q.bread >= 40 && Q.ruble >= 25) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.recovered) {
    RO.add(Q, {bread: 8, ruble: 8, soviet_democracy: 2, bolshevik: -4, right_threat: -2});
} else {
    RO.add(Q, {bread: -3, bolshevik: 5, right_threat: 4, soviet_democracy: -2});
}
!}
go-to: rec_yes if recovered = 1; rec_no if recovered = 0

@rec_yes

= The Republic Is Recovering

By 1920 the harvest has recovered, the railways run and the ruble has stopped falling. The republic has an army that is no longer a danger to itself, a land law that the peasants accept, and an opposition that has to say something other than "Soviet power".

It is not a prosperous country. It is a country in which the bread supply is no longer the first topic of conversation.

@rec_no

= The Republic Is Struggling

By 1920 the harvest is poor, the railways are failing and the ruble has lost most of its remaining value. The republic is a legal government in a hungry country, and every month the opposition on the Left and on the Right says that the experiment has failed.

A government that cannot feed its cities will not survive for ever.
